The following set of commands are the most important ones

r = run
break main => set break point at the function main
b lib1fun => set break point at the function lib1fun

backtrace

#0  bar()  at main.cpp:12
#1  foo()  at main.cpp:7
#2  main() at main.cpp:3

#0 is the current function.

#1 is the function that called it.

#2 is the function that called that one.

step => This is to go inside a function
list => gives you some lines of code above and below the current point we are at. 

frame => tells us where we are currently
ptype a => gives the type of variable a is. 

finish => Runs untill the function returns.

save breakpoints bp.txt
load this at the time of another program by 
source bp.txt






